ential flash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-25T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Southwest San Juan Mountains; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c86447dd54a169ae9df7d6c5b6b9b0c629575548.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c86447dd54a169ae9df7d6c5b6b9b0c629575548.002.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued September 22 at 6:21AM MDT until September 25 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of south central Colorado, including the\nfollowing area, Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Feet.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday afternoon through Thursday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Repeated rounds of moderate to heavy rainfall this week will\nsaturate soils and increase the widespread potential for\nflooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-25T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.faabdd43ae00ea4c6cceab5f555ceaf84269a18b.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.faabdd43ae00ea4c6cceab5f555ceaf84269a18b.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-22T11:22:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 221122 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 522 AM MDT Tue Sep 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Wetter weather returns to the region by Tuesday, with showers and storms possible each day through the end of the work week. - There is a potential for moderate and heavy rainfall that could lead to flooding mainly in the southern San Juans and surrounding","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office